WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.080
Speaker 1: There is a Republican controlled&nbsp;
county in Arizona that is Cochise County or it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.600
may be pronounced goat cheese. It's not completely&nbsp;
clear to me. And they are refusing to certify the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.460
election. As the Associated Press is reporting,&nbsp;
Republican officials in a rural Arizona county&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:23.520
refused yesterday to certify the 2022 election.&nbsp;
Here we go again. It's the same stuff. One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.840
this is the sequel, my friends, a decision&nbsp;
that was quickly challenged in court by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.100
the state's top election official. Now, I&nbsp;
want to make an important distinction here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:39.600
Steve Bannon and some others when it comes to&nbsp;
2020, continue to talk about decertification.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.160
We have to decertify the election. There is no&nbsp;
such process. There's just it doesn't exist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.920
This here is a different situation where they are&nbsp;
saying let's not certify. Certification is indeed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.400
a process. And the secretary of state, Katie&nbsp;
Hobbs, is the Democratic candidate who won and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.400
will be the governor. She has asked the judge to&nbsp;
order county officials to canvass the election,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:11.400
which she said is an obligation under the law.&nbsp;
So there's a couple different things going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.840
here. And of course, no matter what is going on,&nbsp;
these right wingers will come up with some reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.960
why they are actually correct and everything is&nbsp;
absolutely right that they want to do when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.700
want to do it. But any time there's a different&nbsp;
perspective, then it must be somebody who's doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.520
something wrong. It's fraud. It's whatever the&nbsp;
case is going to be. The practice that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:39.240
getting here is to refuse to certify a federal&nbsp;
election. It's important to understand that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.760
are always trial balloons for the next thing, and&nbsp;
refusing to certify a state election at the county&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:52.380
level is a trial for a state refusing to certify&nbsp;
a federal election at the state level. If this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:58.140
were to happen or in any way even a fraction of&nbsp;
it were to happen, they would use it as precedent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:05.400
for the future. That's number one. Secondly, this&nbsp;
isn't legal. Okay. It is absolutely correct to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:11.280
to court to try to force certification. And&nbsp;
these are folks who have been given a duty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:17.400
a task, an election has taken place, the ballots&nbsp;
have been counted. Now you have to certify there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.700
is no analogy to and saying, well, there is&nbsp;
a duty to decertify. Decertification isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.100
a thing. These elected officials have no duty&nbsp;
to decertify elections. You're you're put in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.960
certain position. County Board of elections, you&nbsp;
have to certify they're not doing it. It's a legal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.340
issue. That's why they're going to court. Now, I&nbsp;
know where they are going to ultimately find the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.760
certificate. And it's going to be, of course, in&nbsp;
Hunter Biden's laptop or on Hillary hard drives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.300
emails. Right now, I believe that the grounds here&nbsp;
that they are claiming are, of course, completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:54.960
imaginary. This is going to be certified and&nbsp;
then they are going to say this is proof.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.740
That they stole it because they came in and forced&nbsp;
us to certify something that shouldn't have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:09.120
certified. Of course, it's simply their job to&nbsp;
certify. This is still potentially very dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.120
because almost no matter what ultimately&nbsp;
happens with this attempt not to certify,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.600
they are going to say, well, here's the next&nbsp;
thing that now we have to do at the next election,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.840
which happens to be 2024 presidential, where&nbsp;
Arizona, along with a handful of other states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.040
could determine who's the next president&nbsp;
of the United States. Very scary stuff.

